**Verdict:** revise. Trust is strained, value is useful, delight is a clear hit. Type 3 is the better-supported call and should stay committed; the argument that gets there is weaker than the call.

**Blockers: 1** (plus 7 concerns)

- **ENNEAGRAM-R1:** the childhood origin scene is built on a relocated quote. The draft sets "I could just take control" after her mother's death, "inside that grief and that labor," at age five. The 1985 Time piece puts it on the couch with her sick mother, before the hospital year and the death, so she was about four. The line is also the strongest Type 8 statement in the record, presented as the founding of a Type 3. The same Time piece has the fix: her father paid per A and she "made the most money off of every report card."

**Strongest hit:** the tense reading at line 126 — "'I still have to prove.' Present tense, from the top of the mountain." It is first-person evidence of motive, and it is why the type call holds. The radar line at line 235 is the other one to protect.

**Highest-priority concern:**

- **ENNEAGRAM-C2:** "Why not Type 8?" answers a weakened Eight. It never mentions control, which she, her Vanity Fair profiler, and her daughter all name. Its exhibits fit both types:
  - "Keeps the insults" is not evidence against an Eight; the house Type 8 page lists Vengeance as the Eight's fixation.
  - The 2023 Instagram post is quoted without its "I'm not going to start… Bow down, bitches!" half.
  - "After every backlash she changes the product" fails for 1984 and 1989, and for the 17 months after Sex.
  - The repair is a same-length swap using her own words from just before the thesis quote: "all of my will has always been to conquer some horrible feeling of inadequacy."

One mechanical must-fix sits in the concerns: the thesis blockquote drops a word. Vanity Fair reads "prove that I'm Somebody."

